The photon counting efficiency, \(\varepsilon_{\gamma}\) and fractional purity of the photon sample, \(f_{p}\) are defined by the following relations,

\(\varepsilon_{\gamma}\) = \(N_{\gamma,th}/N_{\gamma,inc}\),

\(f_{p}\) = \(N_{\gamma,th}/N_{\gamma,like}\), where

\(N_{\gamma,inc}\) : number of incident photons from the event generator.

\(N_{\gamma,th}\) : number of photon clusters above the hadron rejection threshold.

\(N_{\gamma,like}\) : total number of clusters above the hadron rejection threshold.

