The azimuthal correlation function for a combination of the trigger and associated particles is defined as

\[D(\Delta\phi)=\frac{1}{N_{trig}}\frac{1}{\epsilon}\int d(\Delta\eta)N(\Delta \phi,\Delta\eta), \tag{4.5}\]

where \(\Delta\phi=\phi^{trig}-\phi^{asso}\), \(N_{trig}\) is the number of particles satisfying the conditions imposed on the trigger particle, and \(\epsilon\) is the reconstruction efficiency of theassociated charged particles. For the \(p_{t}\) range of associated particles used in this analysis (\(p_{t}>1\) GeV/\(c\)) the reconstruction efficiency is about 89% independent of \(p_{t}\) and centrality.

